{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;line-height:107%;\r\nfont-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;The proposed\r\nrear dormer and roof extension, by reason of its excessive size and bulk, would\r\nresult in an overly dominant form of development that would be unduly obtrusive\r\nand incongruous and would detract from the appearance of the subject property\r\nand adjacent properties, to the detriment of the character and appearance of\r\nthe subject property and the surrounding area, contrary to the high quality\r\ndesign aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023, Policy\r\nD3.D.1 and D.11 of The London Plan (2021), Policy CS1.B of the Harrow Core\r\nStrategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Development Management Plan Local Policies\r\n(2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design\r\nGuide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nline-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:\r\nminor-bidi&quot;&gt;The proposal fails to adequately demonstrate that the vehicle\r\ncrossover would allow for the proposed configuration of parking spaces whilst\r\nalso failing to provide accessibility from the public highway. As such, the\r\nproposal would be contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policy D3.D.1 and D.11 of The London\r\nPlan (2021), Policy CS1.B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the\r\nDevelopment Management Plan Local Policies (2013) and the adopted Supplementary\r\nPlanning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-font-kerning:0pt;mso-ligatures:none;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-GB&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nline-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:\r\nminor-bidi&quot;&gt;The proposal, in the absence of a proposed section drawing detailing the internal\r\nhead heights of unit and at first and second floor levels, fails to\r\ndemonstrate that the unit would provide an overall acceptable standard of\r\nliving accommodation in terms of internal head height and total floorspace provision. The local planning authority has therefore been unable to adequately assess residential\r\namenity of future occupiers of the unit, contrary to\r\npolicies DM1 C, DM1 D (g), DM26 A (a), and (c), and DM26 E of the Harrow\r\nDevelopment Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-font-kerning:0pt;mso-ligatures:none;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-GB&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
